    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey prof, i'm really struggling with the intuition behind the fourier transform. i get the formulas, but i don't really \"get\" what's actually happening when a signal gets decomposed into frequencies. can you help me understand the physical intuition of it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Imagine any complex sound wave, like music, as a complex smoothie. The Fourier Transform acts like a specialized blender that takes that smoothie and separates it into its individual ingredients—the pure tones or frequencies it contains. It tells you *how much* of each specific frequency (low bass, mid-range melody, high treble) is present in the original signal. Essentially, it reveals the secret frequency recipe hidden inside the complicated signal.",
